  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let the common tangents to the curves <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;intersect at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>. Let an ellipse, centered at the origin <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>, has lengths of semi-minor and semi-major axes equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>, respectively. If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>e</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math> respectively denote the eccentricity and the length of the latus rectum of this ellipse, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>l</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is equal to ______.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given curves are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></math></p><p>Equation of tangent in slope form to the circle and parabola will be</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#177;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msqrt><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mfenced><mi>i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8943;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Comparing&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>i</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#177;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msqrt><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>here&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;(Rejected)</p><p>so&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p>So, the equation of common tangent will be</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math></p><p>When&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mrow><mi>O</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p>i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Also&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>l</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p>",
